<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Warta</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Warthe</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Warta is a river in western and central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>, about 800 kilometres long and the longest tributary of the Oder. It flows past Sieradz, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poznan">Poznań</a> and Gorzów Wielkopolski and joins the Oder at Kostrzyn. Its basin forms much of Greater Poland, the historic heartland of the early Piast state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/warta.jpg" alt="Warta" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cyku new · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Warta_widziana_z_powietrza_w_okolicach_Mi%C4%99dzychodu_2025.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
